import re
P=".rcs/drafts/v001/paper.md"
t=open(P,encoding="utf-8").read()
def rep(a,b):
    global t
    assert a in t,a[:60]
    t=t.replace(a,b,1)
rep("Researchers used to fixed datasets and fixed evaluation code will recognise the problem: without a shared protocol, two reported numbers are rarely comparable. Here it is sharper because latency and energy, not only accuracy, are part of the result, and both depend on the hardware and software that produced them.","Without a shared protocol, two reported numbers are rarely comparable, and here latency and energy, not only accuracy, are part of the result and depend on the hardware and software that produced them.")
rep("The material supports four contributions, each stated at the strength of its evidence.\n\n1. A specification of four tasks, each with a dataset, a small reference model and a quality target, plus open-source reference implementations {C001, C002, C003}.\n2. A closed/open rule set and a procedure for measuring accuracy, latency and energy of model inference only {C006, C007}.\n3. A host-side runner and optional energy setup that let devices without a file system or display be driven and measured in a standard way {C008}.\n4. A description of the first round: five configurations across microcontrollers, a single-board computer, an accelerator and an FPGA, with observations on numerical formats and on what submitters did and did not change {C010, C011, C012}.","The material supports four contributions:\n\n1. A specification of four tasks with datasets, small reference models and quality targets, plus open-source reference implementations {C001, C002, C003}.\n2. A closed/open rule set and a procedure for measuring accuracy, latency and energy of model inference only {C006, C007}.\n3. A host-side runner and optional energy setup for driving and measuring devices in a standard way {C008}.\n4. A description of the first round: five configurations, with observations on numerical formats and on what submitters did and did not change {C010, C011, C012}.")
rep("**Low power.** Energy is a defining property, so a benchmark should measure it. But devices can consume very different amounts of power, which makes measurement accuracy hard to maintain across the range, and what falls inside the measurement is unclear when data paths and pre-processing differ between devices {C009}.","**Low power.** Energy is a defining property, so a benchmark should measure it; but devices consume very different amounts of power, which makes measurement accuracy hard to maintain, and what falls inside the measurement is unclear when data paths and pre-processing differ {C009}.")
rep("Because devices vary widely, the authors also want several levels of quantization and precision represented. (Quantization stores weights and activations with fewer bits, for instance 8-bit integers instead of 32-bit floating point.) {C009}","The authors also want several levels of quantization (storing weights and activations with fewer bits, such as 8-bit integers instead of 32-bit floating point) represented {C009}.")
rep("These obstacles motivate three design choices that we follow through the paper: small tasks with small models so they fit; a measurement procedure independent of any one software stack; and a division structure that trades comparability against flexibility. The authors also place","The authors also place")
rep(" Section 6 returns to this choice.","")
rep("which lets future results be related to historical data points {C003}.","so future results can be related to historical data points {C003}.")
rep(" They chose this model because it is the DCASE2020 reference, hence a known baseline, and because it adds a model type built only from fully connected layers {C003}."," They chose this model as the DCASE2020 reference, hence a known baseline, and because it adds a model built only from fully connected layers {C003}.")
rep(" The table does not show how sensitive a submitter's result is to the evaluation subset.","")
rep("Submitters pursue different goals: a chip vendor wants to show hardware, a software vendor a toolchain, a research group a better model. The authors therefore use","Submitters pursue different goals (showing hardware, a toolchain or a better model), so the authors use")
rep("The runner lets the user configure a test, detects the hardware, issues commands that load input data and perform measurements, and collects the scores; it also downloads the many input files needed for accuracy measurement {C008}.","The runner configures a test, detects the hardware, issues commands that load input data and perform measurements, collects the scores, and downloads the many input files needed for accuracy measurement {C008}.")
rep(" Other firmware is unchanging boilerplate {C008}.","")
rep("Two configurations exist because energy setup is more complex and energy scores may not be wanted: one for latency and accuracy needs only the host and the device {C008}.","A latency-and-accuracy configuration needs only the host and the device, because the energy setup is more complex and energy scores may not be wanted {C008}.")
rep("the divisions fix what may change, and the framework fixes how measurements are taken. Whether the design permits comparison is addressed by what submitters did with it.","the divisions what may change, and the framework how measurements are taken. Whether the design permits comparison depends on what submitters did with it.")
rep("The authors describe the submitters: an organization showing hardware-agnostic developer tools, a hardware vendor showing its accelerator microarchitecture, an academic institute showing RISC-V microcontrollers for ML, and a multi-disciplinary team showing the open-source hls4ml workflow {C010}.","The authors describe four submitters: an organization showing hardware-agnostic developer tools, a hardware vendor showing its accelerator, an academic institute showing RISC-V microcontrollers, and a team showing the open-source hls4ml workflow {C010}.")
rep(" Table 4 shows five configurations, not five organizations: the baseline row uses the reference platform, and the text describes four submitters {C010}."," The baseline row uses the reference platform, so five configurations are not five organizations {C010}.")
rep("1. **Missing numbers.** Latency and energy values for the reference implementations and any submission results are not in our text, so statements about their range are qualitative {L001}.\n2. **One round, self-selected submitters.** Observations on numerical formats, frameworks and dataset changes describe June 2021 only {L005}.\n3. **Evaluation sets and spread.** Three targets rest on subsets of 200, 1000 and 248 samples, with no spread or repeat count {L002}.\n4. **Inference-only scope.** Streaming and pre-processing are outside the measurement, so latency and energy are those of the model alone {L003}.\n5. **Model coverage.** Closed-division models are mainly fully connected and convolutional; recurrent networks and other architectures are left to the open division or future versions {L004}.\n6. **Energy methodology.** The sampling-frequency statement and the voltage insight are given without supporting measurements {L007}.","1. **Missing numbers.** Latency and energy values and submission results are not in our text, so statements about their range are qualitative {L001}.\n2. **One round, self-selected submitters.** Observations describe June 2021 only {L005}.\n3. **Evaluation sets and spread.** Three targets rest on subsets, with no spread or repeat count {L002}.\n4. **Inference-only scope.** Latency and energy are those of the model alone {L003}.\n5. **Model coverage.** Closed-division models are mainly fully connected and convolutional; recurrent networks are left to the open division or future versions {L004}.\n6. **Energy methodology.** The sampling-frequency statement and the voltage insight lack supporting measurements {L007}.")
rep("They suggest a collaborative community could help create standards for responsible deployment. These are statements of expectation, not outcomes measured in the paper.","These are statements of expectation, not measured outcomes.")
rep("For a reader from another subfield, what changes is a set of concrete conventions: which tasks and targets stand in for TinyML, what counts as the measured window, and which components a submitter may change. What remains","What remains")
